1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Project name: ACMS

Full form: AICTE Approval & Compliance Management System

Project context: Smart India Hackathon prototype

Core purpose: Design a unified digital workflow that helps technical institutions manage approval applications, submit supporting evidence, respond to deficiencies, track scrutiny, coordinate Expert Visit Committee activities where applicable, view authorized decisions, and manage post-approval regulatory obligations.

The platform should improve traceability, reduce repetitive administrative work, make application status easier to understand, and help institutions maintain compliance records.

Core innovation

Implement a proposed feature called ROEG — Regulatory Obligation & Evidence Graph.

ROEG connects:

- Regulatory requirements and their versions
- Applications and institutions
- Required documents and submitted evidence
- Evidence versions and extracted information
- Verification checks and results
- Deficiencies and corrective actions
- Responsible users and deadlines
- EVC records where applicable
- Authorized decisions
- Post-approval obligations
- Audit events and change history

Also implement Dependency-Aware Incremental Re-Scrutiny. When a document or applicable rule changes, the system should identify which checks depend on that change and rerun only those checks when dependencies are known and unchanged inputs are verifiable. If dependencies are uncertain, trigger a full revalidation.

Present this as a proposed workflow innovation to be evaluated, not as a proven industry-first capability.

AI boundaries

AI can assist with document OCR, metadata extraction, document classification, evidence-to-requirement matching, and explanations of detected deficiencies.

AI must never autonomously grant or reject regulatory approval. All consequential scrutiny findings must be reviewable, and final decisions must be recorded by an authorized human officer.

