Institution isolation

Institution users may only access records linked to institutions for which they have an authorized membership.

Officer isolation

Officers may access only records permitted by their assigned scope and permissions.

EVC isolation

EVC users may access only the assigned cases and necessary related records.

Approving official isolation

Authorized officials may access cases within their configured authority and scope.

Administrator access

System administrators receive only the permissions required for system administration. All privileged operations must be audited.

Storage access

Evidence files must be private.

Implement access policies for:

- Uploading evidence
- Reading evidence
- Downloading evidence
- Replacing evidence
- Accessing superseded versions

Validate permissions in backend functions and storage policies, not only in frontend code.

Security requirements

- Never put service-role keys in frontend code.
- Validate inputs server-side.
- Restrict file size and permitted formats.
- Use safe filenames and storage keys.
- Protect against unauthorized direct-object access.
- Avoid logging passwords, secrets, and unnecessary sensitive document contents.
- Use secure session management.
- Rate-limit sensitive operations where practical.
- Preserve audit history.
- Apply least privilege.
- Use private storage and short-lived signed URLs where appropriate.

Do not claim that the prototype is certified or legally compliant without an actual assessment.

