29. FUNCTIONAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

Do not consider the build complete until the following are implemented and tested.

Authentication

- Users can sign in and sign out.
- Routes are protected.
- Roles are enforced.
- Privileged roles cannot be self-assigned.

Applications

- An institution can create and save a draft.
- A draft can be edited after saving.
- Required fields are validated.
- A valid application can be submitted.
- Status history is recorded.

Documents

- A valid file can be uploaded to private storage.
- Invalid files are rejected.
- Evidence metadata is persisted.
- New versions do not erase previous history.
- Unauthorized users cannot download another institution's documents.

Scrutiny

- Officers can review assigned applications.
- Verification results are persisted.
- Deficiencies can be raised.
- Institutions can respond and resubmit.
- Resubmission history is preserved.

Incremental re-scrutiny

- Changing evidence identifies dependent checks.
- Unaffected checks are reused only when all required version and dependency conditions remain valid.
- Uncertain dependencies trigger full revalidation.
- The result and reason are recorded.
- Incremental results agree with full recomputation on the defined test cases.

EVC and decisions

- EVC records can be created and submitted by permitted users.
- Authorized officials can record decisions.
- Unauthorized users cannot record decisions.
- Decision reasons and audit events persist.

Compliance

- Applicable obligations can be assigned.
- Evidence can be submitted.
- Review status can change through permitted transitions.
- Overdue status is calculated from configured deadlines.

Reports and audit

- Dashboard metrics are derived from stored data.
- Filters work.
- Authorized CSV exports work.
- Audit events are visible to permitted users.

Quality

- No broken routes.
- No dead buttons.
- No fake success messages.
- No hardcoded secrets.
- No public exposure of confidential files.
- No reliance on frontend-only authorization.
- No misleading claims that demo OCR or official integrations are live.

